# The OpenAPI snapshot + generated types are byte-compared against a
# fresh openapi-typescript run by `pnpm openapi:check` (string equality,
# line endings included). The generator always emits LF, so these files
# must stay LF on EVERY platform -- a CRLF checkout makes the drift
# check fail on every line. (The original blob was committed CRLF from
# a Windows working tree, which broke the check on all Linux checkouts.)
src/lib/openapi-types.gen.ts text eol=lf
src/lib/openapi-snapshot.json text eol=lf

# The generated route tree is a tracked release-build input and is likewise
# compared byte-for-byte after regeneration.
src/routeTree.gen.ts text eol=lf
